Stub is a static app, not a Jekyll site.

Without this file GitHub Pages runs every push through Jekyll before publishing. That
buys nothing here — there are no layouts, no posts and no Liquid templates — and it adds
a build step that can fail silently: when it does, Pages keeps serving the previous build
and reports success, so a deploy appears to have worked while the live site is unchanged.
Which is exactly what happened to v87, stuck behind v85 for half an hour with every
commit correct on the branch.

The file's presence is the whole signal; its contents are ignored.
